// cases_canvas.cla: Canvas (Task 7, ui-scenario-retirement batch) -- the
// migrated replacement for the retired testdata/ui/canvas.cla golden UI
// scenario: a buffered canvas animated by a top-level `every 4 ticks`
// block (a 20x20 filled square sliding right), asserted by the retired
// suite purely as "two snaps taken after different amounts of ticking
// differ" (internal/mactest/ui_test.go's own checkCanvasSnaps, no other
// Go-side invariant, confirmed before writing this case). See harness.
// cla's own CanvasWin comment for the window/every-block transcription
// (unchanged cadence: `every 4 ticks`, same dx=3 step).
//
// UiTestTick(n)'s scripted-mode path forwards to the SAME "tick n" verb
// (rtUiScriptDispatchLine -> rtUiScriptTick, uiscript.cla) a `.events`
// script line would dispatch -- there is no separate "test-mode" every-
// pump logic, so a window opened MID-CASE (this case runs inside
// RunAll's own dispatch, not at App.launch like the retired fixture's own
// `on App.launch { open Anim }`) still gets its `every` block pumped
// correctly: rtUiScriptEveryPump (uiscript.cla) iterates the global
// rtUiEveryDueArr and fires whatever's due purely by elapsed virtual-tick
// count, with no dependency on which window is frontmost or when it was
// opened. `CanvasWin.front` (the every-block's own guard) is "the
// frontmost OPEN INSTANCE of type CanvasWin" (language reference: "Doc.
// front is the frontmost open instance of type Doc"), not "the frontmost
// window overall" -- so it resolves correctly even while this suite's own
// Suite window is the actual frontmost window on screen throughout.
//
// DISCOVERED RUNTIME QUIRK (pre-existing, not introduced by this task;
// see task-7-report.md's own "concerns" section for the full escalation):
// `rtUiBuildEvery` (ui.cla, called once from `rtUiStartup`, itself called
// by the compiler-generated entry sequence BEFORE `App.launch`/`App.
// startEmpty` or the scripted event loop ever run) seeds every every-
// block's INITIAL `due` tick as `now + interval`, where `now` is supposed
// to be `0` for any `--events`-compiled build (`peekb(UiTestScript()) !=
// 0`) so the schedule is virtual-tick-based throughout. Empirically
// (peekl(rtUiEveryDueArr) read directly from this case, before this case
// does anything else), THIS suite's own composed build measured an
// initial due of 50, not 4 -- consistent with `now` having actually been
// a REAL `UiTickCount()` value (~46, plausible for how long this SUITE's
// own larger startup -- many more windows/menus than the retired
// standalone canvas.cla fixture ever built -- takes before reaching that
// point) rather than 0, even though `UiTestTick`'s OWN (later-executing)
// `if rtUiScripted` gate correctly detects and uses the virtual-tick path
// (confirmed: this case's own tick calls advance rtUiVirtualTicks in
// lockstep, exactly `+4` per call, with no drift). The retired standalone
// fixture never surfaced this because its own real boot-time tick count
// at that early point was apparently small enough to fall within its own
// script's tick budget (8 x `tick 4` = 32) by coincidence -- a byte-exact
// blessed golden just captures whatever really happened, bug or not, and
// nothing about mac-target-4b's own review ever isolated the every-
// block's OWN initial-due arithmetic to notice.
//
// Workaround (NOT a fake -- it drives the exact same real mechanism,
// through the same public UiTestTick API, all the way to a state where it
// behaves exactly as documented): a single generously-oversized warm-up
// UiTestTick call, BEFORE the real measured cadence, guarantees crossing
// ANY plausible real-boot-tick-seeded due (scripted ticks cost no real
// wall-clock time at all, so a big n is free) and fires the block once
// (a harmless, discarded x+=dx bump); rtUiScriptEveryPump's own reschedule
// after that fire (`due = rtUiVirtualTicks + interval`) is unconditionally
// virtual-tick-based, so every firing from then on behaves exactly as
// designed -- confirmed empirically (see task-7-report.md).
//
// A tick's every-pump fires each due entry AT MOST ONCE per UiTestTick
// call, regardless of the `n` passed (same "at most once per tick N
// script line" contract canvas.events' own header comment documents) --
// so, after the warm-up, this case calls UiTestTick(4) three times (not
// UiTestTick(12) once) to get three firings before the first checksum,
// mirroring canvas.events' own "tick 4" x3 cadence exactly, then five
// more calls before the second checksum (canvas.events' own "tick 4" x5).

// tbCanvasWarmupTicks: see this file's own header comment on the
// discovered runtime quirk -- large enough to clear any plausible real
// boot-time tick count (a few hundred ticks is several real seconds; this
// suite's own measured value was ~46) with a wide safety margin, and free
// (no real wall-clock cost) since it is entirely virtual-tick arithmetic
// under a scripted boot.
const tbCanvasWarmupTicks: int = 2000

// tbCanvasCkX0/Y0/W/H: an 8px-aligned checksum region that fully contains
// the sliding square at BOTH sampled positions. CanvasWin's `size: 160,
// 160` -> content top-left ((512-160)/2, 44) = (176, 44) (already a
// multiple of 8, no local-offset adjustment needed). The square is a
// 20x20 fill at LOCAL (x, 60); x is 19 after 3 firings past the warm-up's
// own one bump (10 + 3*3) and 34 after 8 firings past it (19 + 3*5) --
// see this file's own header comment. LOCAL x=16 (176+16=192, a multiple
// of 8) through LOCAL x=56 (176+56=232, a multiple of 8, width 40) fully
// contains both squares' bounding boxes (19..39 and 34..54, both inside
// [16,56]) with margin on every side.
const tbCanvasCkX0: int = 192
const tbCanvasCkY0: int = 104
const tbCanvasCkW: int = 40
const tbCanvasCkH: int = 20

func caseCanvas(): TestResult {
    var w: CanvasWin
    var i: int
    var s1: int
    var s2: int
    var detail: string

    w = open CanvasWin

    // Warm-up: see this file's own header comment. Discards its own
    // (harmless) one-time effect on x -- only the s1/s2 DIFFERENCE below
    // is asserted, not any absolute x value.
    UiTestTick(tbCanvasWarmupTicks)

    i = 0
    while i < 3 {
        UiTestTick(4)
        i = i + 1
    }
    s1 = UiTestChecksum(tbCanvasCkX0, tbCanvasCkY0, tbCanvasCkW, tbCanvasCkH)

    i = 0
    while i < 5 {
        UiTestTick(4)
        i = i + 1
    }
    s2 = UiTestChecksum(tbCanvasCkX0, tbCanvasCkY0, tbCanvasCkW, tbCanvasCkH)

    close w

    if s1 != s2 {
        return tkPass("Canvas")
    }
    detail = "s1 " + tkIntToStr(s1) + " == s2 " + tkIntToStr(s2)
    return tkFail("Canvas", detail)
}
